        "content": "Read one document and report what it says in answer to a question. Use only this document: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no guesses.\n\nQuestion: When did Attorney General Lawrence serve in his position?\n\nDocument:\nPremier of Ontario Bill Davis ( 1971–1985 ) Bill Davis Philip Andrewes Syl Apps George Ashe James Auld Reuben Baetz Dalton Bales Richard B. Beckett Claude Bennett Leo Bernier Margaret Birch Andy Brandt René Brunelle Gordon Carton John Clement Gordon Dean Frank Drea Robert G. Eaton Robert Elgie Susan Fish Bud Gregory Allan Grossman Larry Grossman Fernand Guindon Sid Handleman Lorne Henderson Donald Irvine George Kerr Allan Lawrence Bert Lawrence Nick Leluk John MacBeth Charles MacNaughton Lorne Maeck Bruce McCaffrey George McCague Darcy McKeough Roy McMurtry Jack McNie Arthur Meen Frank Miller Robert C. Mitchell Bill Newman Keith Norton Harry\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"relevant\": true, \"cards\": [{\"entity\": \"\", \"sense\": \"\", \"answer\": \"\", \"as_of\": \"\", \"claim_kind\": \"\", \"attributed_to\": \"\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"claim\": \"\"}]}\n\n\"relevant\": false if the document is about some other topic and is of no use for the question; then \"cards\" is [].\n\"cards\": one card for each answer the document itself gives to the question. Usually that is one card. It is several cards if the document gives several answers, such as a list of names: one card each. It is [] if the document gives no answer. The question may fit several things that share a name: whichever of them this document is about, report its answer. If the document only says that some answer is wrong, write no card for that answer.\n\nThe fields of a card:\n- \"entity\": who or what this answer is about, as specifically as the document identifies it: the full name, plus the details the document gives that tell it apart from others with the same name (what kind of thing it is, profession or role, nationality or place, years, creator,